## BINDING HOLD
HPSM-POC deploys nothing: no `az`, no docker push, no ssh, no HTTP to any hosted, demo, UAT or production host (every measurement is on the local mock build or a local API). A local SQL Server container for the test run is allowed, on a host port in your block only, the password as an environment variable only (never on a command line, never printed). **You open no PR; Tuesday lands it through CodeQL (never bypass, never dismiss) and deploys to the hosted site after landing in a separate kit.** No Jira write; no message to any human. Never delete (quarantine to `.tools/b1535/_quarantine/`; a container you started is stopped and removed by id); no force-push, amend, reset or rebase. **Never type `cd`.** No migration, no API contract change, no package change, no `web/scripts/**` change, no workflow (`.github/**`) change, no content-package change. This phase builds no integration with HP tools (Security Manager API, Fleet Threat Assessment, firmware tools, SIEM); next-phase items are stored and architected only, and none of this is ever shown to HP as done. **The words are the product owner's, copied, not composed:** you add no word that is not in a FROZEN line. The journey rename, the landing copy, the report introduction, the three operating modes, Good/Better/Best packages, the commercial stages and the coach (the C rows), and the deck's own sentences (K2, K3, `content/packages/`, `content/client/`, `api/.../SeedContent/`) are not built and not touched.

