## THE LOOP (every part; this is "red-first" for text pinned by tests)
1. In `head`, apply the part's FROZEN rows to the product files. Run the part's test files UNCHANGED: the tests that pin the old words go RED. Print each red test name and count, and match them to the pin tables below (a red the tables do not name is printed with its cause and fixed in the same part if it pins a changed string; a red that pins nothing you changed is a STOP).
2. Rewrite each red pin's literal **from the rendered page, not by hand**: take vitest's received text (for the whole-page tests) and accept it only after a hunk-to-row map is printed (diff the old literal against the received text; every hunk maps to FROZEN row ids; an unmapped hunk is a STOP). Small pins (a name, a heading, a substring) are changed to the FROZEN `new` text by a program or a one-line edit shown in STATUS.
3. Run the same files again in `head`: GREEN (print passed / failed). Then copy ONLY the updated test files into `mut` (main's product files) and run them: they must be RED there, and every red named: this is the red-first proof. Restore `mut` (by blob from main) after.
4. One commit per part (P1, P2, P3) after its proofs are green; plain push of the branch (see MOVED MAIN).

